cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Engineer Paper Radar in your research or teaching, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Engineer Paper Radar: Automated Literature Intelligence, Verification Filtering, and Federated Curation"
abstract: >-
  A local, stdlib-only Python radar for new research papers. It collects IEEE, Crossref, OpenAlex,
  arXiv, PubMed and bioRxiv/medRxiv records, scores them against the reader's own research pillars
  (keywords, VIP authors, anchors, bibliographic coupling and a personal taste model), flags
  measured-silicon or wet-lab evidence against simulation-only work, builds an interactive dashboard
  and weekly reports, and lets collaborators federate a shared corpus through user-owned private Git
  data repos. Formerly IC Paper Radar; domain presets cover IC/ECE, general engineering and robotics,
  biomedicine and chemistry/materials. Contributors: Daidingxx (arXiv source connector).
authors:
